Demand
    some concepts may use:
        - market: is any arrangement that enalbes buyers and sellers to get infromation and do business with each other
        - competivtive market: the market that has many buyer and sellers so no single buyer or seller can influrence the price
        - money price: is the amount of money needed to buy ti
        - relatice price: the ratio of its money price to the money price of its opportunity cost
        - wants: the unlimited sesires or wishes people have for goods and services

    demand something always means:
        1. want it
        2. be able to afford it
        3. have made a definite plan to buy it

    quantity demanded:
        a good or service is the amount that consumers plan to buy during a particular time period and at a particular price
            1. plan to buy: doesn't mean the goods/services had been bought
            2. dimension of time: it indicates during a given period of time, at a particular price.

    Law of demand:
        other things remaininng the same, the higher the price of a good, the smaller is the quantity demanded.    

    Law of demand based on two reasons:
        - subsititution effect: whan an increase in the relative price of a good/services occurs, consumers will purchase less of the good or service and more of a substitute.
        - income effect: when an increase in the relative price of a good/service occurs, consumers have less money to spend on all goods and services, including the good or service whose price increased

    Demand curve:
        demand curve refers to the entire relationship btw the prices of a good or sercive and the quantity demanded ceteris paribus. 

        Price
            | \
            |  \
            |   \ demand curve
            |    \
            |_____\________ Quantity

        In addition, we can also refer to the demand curve as:
            willingness and ability to pay curve or the marginal benefit curve
            -> this means with more quantity consumers buy, the marginal benefit will diminish

        note: only the price will influence demand curve. other factors except price will chenge demand itself.


    
    Demand factors:
        based on the factor, the demand curve will shift to right or left, which means the demand itself is influenced.
            - when demand increases, the demand curve shifts rightward
            - when demand decreases, the demand curve shifts leftward

        there are six main factors may change demand:
            1. the prices of related goods:
                - Subsititutes goods: the goods can be used in place of another good, like margarine and butter
                - Component goods: the goods that is used in conjunction with another good, like sugar and tea

                if subsititutes price increases, the demand will increase; if decreases, the demand will decrease

                if component price increases, the demand will decreases; if decreases, the demand will increase
            
            2. expected future prices
                if the price of a good is expected to rise in the future, the current demand for it increases, and the curve shifts rightward, like investment

            3. income
                - normal good: the good that demand increases as income increases
                - inferior good: the good that demand decreases as income increases, like instant noodles

                based on the income increases/decreases, the demand will change along with its change.
            
            4. expected future income and credit
                if expected future income and credit increases, then consumers will purchase more goods

            5. population
                the larger the population, the greater is the demand for all goods

            6. preference
                Demand will increase if perferences increase; demand shifts rightward.




